# A `params: [...]` frontmatter key (kexhq/kex#171 M3) fixes the generated
# function's parameter names AND order explicitly, overriding free-variable
# inference — the same list `Template.scan`'s own `Parsed#parameters`
# already parses (kexhq/kex#252, M1). The body's own reading order is
# `count` then `title`; the frontmatter declares the opposite, and the call
# below only works in the FRONTMATTER's order — proving that order won,
# not inference's first-appearance one.

main do
  let show = Template.text(`---
params: [title, count]
---
<%= count %> of <%= title %>`)
  IO.printLine(show("Items", 3))
end
